      <div class="frame-body">
        <p class="lede" style="margin: 0 0 20px; white-space: nowrap; font-size: 30px;">The session is meant to last 30 minutes, but active users get logged out after about 30 seconds.</p>
        <div class="shots compact">
          <div class="shot">
            <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><small>localhost · /#0003</small></div>
            <img src="assets/app-signedin.png" alt="Snippet bin signed in as admin, viewing a snippet">
            <div class="cap">
              <span class="tag ok"><i></i>Signed in, working</span>
              <p>Logged in as admin, reading a snippet. Everything is fine.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="shot bad">
            <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><small>localhost · my snippets</small></div>
            <img src="assets/app-expired.png" alt="Snippet bin login screen showing a session expired message">
            <div class="cap">
              <span class="tag warn"><i></i>About 30 seconds later</span>
              <p>One click after a short pause: kicked out, asked to sign in again.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="callout">The timeout itself is correct. The real cause hides in how each request <strong>refreshes the session</strong>, across more than one file. You will trace it in Lab 0 and Lab A1.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
